                <pb facs="0427" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg357"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/2297: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-17T19:00:00-04:00">May 17, 1934—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>49. Your 85, May 16, midnight. We are expressing at Bogotá and at Lima our
                    opinion that the Mello Franco compromise formula, with the proposals he has made
                    to cover the remaining two points, is equitable and offers an honorable and
                    peaceful method of reaching a permanent solution of this controversy. We have
                    expressed hope that the formula may be accepted by both Colombia and Peru.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
